  "description": "March 30, 2025 – Alibaba, Latin America & Nvidia Breakdown",
  "body_html": "<p>Overall, the general stock market and the magnificent 7…have <em><strong>not</strong></em> been so “magnificent”. However there are several mid caps and small caps that have shown extreme strength throughout the the recent S&amp;P 500 plummets. Be sure to check out the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/timothys-stocks-ea4\">StockTok</a> tracker for updates on positions. </p><p>The ES1! futures showed a strong upward bounce early in the week, however erased those gains by end of last week. Fortunately, no newer lows have been formed…so there is hope. But hope is not a strategy ❌. Should price break below $5580, it is very likely the general market continues trending down. A break above $5830 would provide higher conviction of a trend upwards. Recall, this was the very bounce we have had since the decline from mid-February. Let the price action determine your actions!</p><p>Our positions showed extreme strength, rising more than large caps yet declining less during the drops. This is great should the overall market reverse. My speculation is that the market is just pricing in <em><strong>fear </strong></em>of the Tariffs…and that April 2nd may actually be a reversal time. </p><p>Read on to see updates on our positions along with Nvidia, Alibaba and Latin America 👇</p>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
  "truncated_body_text": "Overall, the general stock market and the magnificent 7…have not been so “magnificent”. However there are several mid caps and small caps that have shown extreme strength throughout the the recent S&P 500 plummets. Be sure to check out the StockTok tracker for updates on positions.",
